, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How do I greet someone on a business call in Japanese?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "お世話になっております (osewa ni natte orimasu) is the standard greeting for people you’ve worked with before, followed by your name and company. For first-time contacts or customers, お電話ありがとうございます (odenwa arigatou gozaimasu) is the usual choice.

"
}
}
, {
"@type": "Question",
"name": "How do I ask to speak with a specific person?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Use a polite phrase like 山田さんはいらっしゃいますでしょうか？ (Yamada-san wa irasshaimasu deshouka?), meaning “Is Mr. Yamada available?” Adding 話させていただいてよろしいでしょうか (may I speak with him?) makes it even more polite.

