"name": "Do I need to use keigo when calling a restaurant or delivery company?",
"acceptedAnswer": {
"@type": "Answer",
"text": "Yes, it’s best to use polite Japanese. Phrases like 予約をしたいのですが (I’d like to make a reservation) and 〜をお願いしたいのですが (I’d like to request ~) sound natural and respectful, and staff will typically respond in keigo.

